Fix camera/shape transform doubled when a USD ancestor already has an authored transform

UsdArnoldPrimWriter::_WriteMatrix() cancels an exported node's own baked world
matrix against an ancestor's transform by walking up the USD hierarchy looking
for an ancestor prim that matches an Arnold node by name. When the ancestor was
instead authored directly by *another* writer/tool - e.g. mayaUsd's own native
-defaultCameras export, which writes persp/top/front/side as plain Xform prims
with real authored transforms and no matching Arnold node - the loop found no
match and skipped cancellation entirely, so the child's own world matrix
composed on top of the ancestor's authored transform, doubling it (MTOA-3064).

This test reproduces that scenario directly with AiSceneWrite's "append" mode:
data/existing.usda stands in for a stage a previous writer already touched (an
Xform with an authored transform and no matching Arnold node), and the test
appends a single Arnold polymesh underneath it. It then parses the resulting
USD text, composes the child's authored matrix with the ancestor's own
authored transform exactly like USD would when consuming the stage, and checks
the result against the node's actual intended world position. Before the fix,
the composed result is off by the ancestor's transform.

author: Ashley Handscomb Retallack
